bottomparticipants

actor User
boundary "Login Page" as UI
boundary Router
control AuthController
control AuthService
control GoogleOAuth

User -> UI: 1. Click "Login with Google"
activate User
activate UI

UI -> GoogleOAuth: 2. Open Google login popup
activate GoogleOAuth

GoogleOAuth --> UI: 3. Return idToken
deactivate GoogleOAuth

UI -> Router: 4. POST /api/auth/google (idToken)
activate Router

Router -> AuthController: 5. loginWithGoogle(idToken)
activate AuthController

AuthController -> AuthService: 6. loginWithGoogle(idToken)
activate AuthService

AuthService -> GoogleOAuth: 7. verifyIdToken(idToken)
activate GoogleOAuth

GoogleOAuth --> AuthService: 8. token payload
deactivate GoogleOAuth

AuthService -> AuthService: 9. Check token
activate AuthService
space
deactivate AuthService

alt Invalid Google token
    AuthService --> AuthController: 9.1.1 Throw UnauthorizedException
    AuthController --> Router: 9.1.2 HTTP 401 response
    Router --> UI: 9.1.3 Show authentication error
    UI --> User: 9.1.4 Google login failed
else Email missing or not verified
    AuthService --> AuthController: 9.2.1 Throw UnauthorizedException
    AuthController --> Router: 9.2.2 HTTP 401 response
    Router --> UI: 9.2.3 Show verification error
    UI --> User: 9.2.4 Google email not verified
end

ref over AuthService: 3.6.b.i. Subsequence - Find user for Google Login

AuthService --> AuthController: 10. Return accessToken & tokenPayload
deactivate AuthService
deactivate AuthService

AuthController --> Router: 11. Set HTTP-only cookie (access_token)
deactivate AuthController

Router --> UI: 12. Login success response
deactivate Router

UI --> User: 13. Redirect to home page
deactivate UI
deactivate User